1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,932
There are only four ways to lose
points on SAT linear word problems.

2
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:06,698
You mix up the slope
and the starting value.

3
00:00:06,718 --> 00:00:10,396
You start from the wrong row of a table.

4
00:00:10,611 --> 00:00:13,325
You round up when the
answer has to round down.

5
00:00:13,646 --> 00:00:15,861
And the fourth one looks completely right,

6
00:00:15,968 --> 00:00:19,040
because every number in it
comes from the equation.

7
00:00:19,063 --> 00:00:20,813
The first three are quick to fix.

8
00:00:21,205 --> 00:00:23,543
The fourth is a rate
rewritten in new units,

9
00:00:23,563 --> 00:00:25,492
like liters every forty minutes.

10
00:00:26,169 --> 00:00:28,526
That's question six, the hardest one.

11
00:00:28,884 --> 00:00:33,489
Stay for it, because three of the choices
use the right numbers the wrong way.

12
00:00:33,509 --> 00:00:37,239
One habit handles all four:
say what each number means,

13
00:00:37,259 --> 00:00:39,224
with its units, before you pick.

14
00:00:39,438 --> 00:00:42,845
Six practice questions, each
one harder than the last.

15
00:00:42,865 --> 00:00:45,831
Keep score as you go, and
see if you can get all six.

16
00:00:45,892 --> 00:00:49,213
Every linear function looks
like y equals m x plus b.

17
00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:51,892
In a word problem,
those letters have jobs.

18
00:00:52,677 --> 00:00:57,713
m is the rate: how much y changes
for each one unit increase in x.

19
00:00:58,285 --> 00:01:02,499
b is the starting value:
what y is when x is zero.

20
00:01:02,574 --> 00:01:04,161
Here's an example.

21
00:01:04,181 --> 00:01:09,145
A gym charges a forty dollar sign-up
fee plus twenty-five dollars per month.

22
00:01:09,466 --> 00:01:13,089
The total cost is C equals
twenty-five m plus forty,

23
00:01:13,109 --> 00:01:14,966
where m is the number of months.

24
00:01:15,013 --> 00:01:16,350
Twenty-five is the slope.

25
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:20,457
Its units are dollars per month, so the
cost goes up twenty-five dollars for

26
00:01:20,477 --> 00:01:21,477
each month.

27
00:01:21,727 --> 00:01:23,441
Forty is the intercept.

28
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:27,620
When m is zero, before any
months, you've paid forty dollars.

29
00:01:27,869 --> 00:01:29,155
That's the sign-up fee.

30
00:01:29,229 --> 00:01:31,694
Use these two sentences
for any linear model.

31
00:01:32,657 --> 00:01:36,602
For a slope: for each
one unit increase in x,

32
00:01:36,622 --> 00:01:38,351
y changes by the slope.

33
00:01:38,371 --> 00:01:41,015
If the slope is negative, y goes down.

34
00:01:41,587 --> 00:01:45,015
For an intercept: when x is
zero, y equals the intercept.

35
00:01:45,153 --> 00:01:46,847
The SAT tests this in three main ways.

36
00:01:46,867 --> 00:01:51,525
First, interpretation: what does
this number mean in context?

37
00:01:51,545 --> 00:01:58,473
Second, building: write the equation
from a description or a table.

38
00:01:58,545 --> 00:02:02,740
Third, inequalities: at most, at least,

39
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:04,545
and which values are possible.

40
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:07,142
Interpretation questions come up a lot,

41
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:09,820
and they usually look like this.

42
00:02:10,677 --> 00:02:14,677
What is the best interpretation
of twelve in this context?

43
00:02:15,534 --> 00:02:17,800
Every answer choice sounds reasonable,

44
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:20,142
so you have to test each
one against the equation.

45
00:02:20,205 --> 00:02:21,312
Question one.

46
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:27,383
The equation V equals twelve t plus
one hundred fifty gives the volume V,

47
00:02:27,526 --> 00:02:32,919
in gallons, of water in a tank t minutes
after a pump starts filling the tank.

48
00:02:33,061 --> 00:02:36,598
What is the best interpretation
of twelve in this context?

49
00:02:36,649 --> 00:02:37,721
Pause and try it.

50
00:02:40,965 --> 00:02:43,266
Twelve is the coefficient
of t, so it's the slope,

51
00:02:43,286 --> 00:02:44,766
and slope is a rate.

52
00:02:44,786 --> 00:02:47,124
Its units are the y units per x unit:

53
00:02:47,144 --> 00:02:48,301
gallons per minute.

54
00:02:48,321 --> 00:02:51,481
So each minute, the volume
goes up by twelve gallons.

55
00:02:51,501 --> 00:02:52,924
The answer is B.

56
00:02:52,944 --> 00:02:54,051
Test the others.

57
00:02:54,551 --> 00:02:57,086
A says the tank started
with twelve gallons.

58
00:02:57,372 --> 00:02:59,602
But the starting amount
is V when t is zero,

59
00:02:59,622 --> 00:03:01,051
which is one hundred fifty.

60
00:03:01,158 --> 00:03:03,514
D says twelve gallons after one minute,

61
00:03:03,622 --> 00:03:05,835
but V of one is one hundred sixty-two.

62
00:03:06,014 --> 00:03:07,575
And C is wrong too.

63
00:03:07,595 --> 00:03:10,575
Adding one hundred fifty gallons
takes twelve and a half minutes,

64
00:03:10,595 --> 00:03:10,909
not twelve.

65
00:03:10,929 --> 00:03:11,965
Question two.

66
00:03:12,572 --> 00:03:17,088
A hiker's distance d, in miles, from the
end of a trail h hours after she starts

67
00:03:17,108 --> 00:03:21,428
hiking is given by d equals
fourteen minus two point five h.

68
00:03:21,857 --> 00:03:25,608
What is the best interpretation
of fourteen in this context?

69
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:26,710
Pause and try it.

70
00:03:29,955 --> 00:03:33,812
Fourteen is the constant, so it's
the value of d when h is zero.

71
00:03:33,883 --> 00:03:38,327
At the moment she starts hiking, she's
fourteen miles from the end of the trail.

72
00:03:38,347 --> 00:03:40,311
The answer is C.

73
00:03:40,392 --> 00:03:41,892
Two point five is the rate.

74
00:03:42,427 --> 00:03:45,428
She gets two point five
miles closer every hour.

75
00:03:45,750 --> 00:03:48,693
So A, which calls fourteen her speed,

76
00:03:48,713 --> 00:03:51,015
is wrong, and so is B.

77
00:03:51,035 --> 00:03:54,801
She covers two point five
miles in the first hour,

78
00:03:54,821 --> 00:03:56,730
not fourteen.

79
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:58,392
D is wrong too.

80
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:02,678
Fourteen divided by two point
five is five point six hours.

81
00:04:02,716 --> 00:04:04,038
Question three.

82
00:04:04,538 --> 00:04:07,895
A student deposits the same amount
into a savings account each week.

83
00:04:08,359 --> 00:04:11,038
The table shows the amount A, in dollars,

84
00:04:11,108 --> 00:04:14,466
in the account w weeks after the
student started making deposits.

85
00:04:15,323 --> 00:04:17,609
At two weeks, it's three
hundred forty dollars.

86
00:04:18,109 --> 00:04:19,930
At five weeks, four hundred forty-five.

87
00:04:20,538 --> 00:04:22,966
At nine weeks, five hundred eighty-five.

88
00:04:23,787 --> 00:04:26,038
Which equation represents
this relationship?

89
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,170
Pause and try it.

90
00:04:31,415 --> 00:04:32,843
Find the slope first.

91
00:04:33,058 --> 00:04:36,716
From week two to week five, the amount
goes from three hundred forty to four

92
00:04:36,736 --> 00:04:37,986
hundred forty-five.

93
00:04:38,093 --> 00:04:40,394
That's one hundred five
dollars over three weeks,

94
00:04:40,414 --> 00:04:42,304
or thirty-five dollars per week.

95
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:43,502
Now the intercept.

96
00:04:44,502 --> 00:04:46,824
Work back from week two to week zero.

97
00:04:47,752 --> 00:04:50,216
Two weeks at thirty-five
dollars is seventy,

98
00:04:50,573 --> 00:04:53,160
and three hundred forty minus
seventy is two hundred seventy.

99
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:57,357
So A equals thirty-five w
plus two hundred seventy.

100
00:04:57,377 --> 00:04:59,199
The answer is A.

101
00:04:59,662 --> 00:05:03,465
Check week nine: thirty-five times
nine is three hundred fifteen,

102
00:05:03,485 --> 00:05:06,127
plus two hundred seventy is
five hundred eighty-five.

103
00:05:06,189 --> 00:05:07,761
B is the big trap.

104
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:11,098
It uses three hundred forty
as the starting value,

105
00:05:11,118 --> 00:05:14,046
but that's the amount at
week two, not week zero.

106
00:05:14,975 --> 00:05:17,775
C uses one hundred five,
the change in dollars,

107
00:05:17,795 --> 00:05:19,868
without dividing by the change in weeks.

108
00:05:20,975 --> 00:05:23,154
It fits the first row and nothing else.

109
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:23,883
Desmos shortcut.

110
00:05:23,903 --> 00:05:28,847
Add a table and enter the weeks
as x one and the dollars as y one.

111
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:33,724
Then type y one, tilde, m x one plus b.

112
00:05:34,617 --> 00:05:38,403
Desmos returns m equals thirty-five
and b equals two hundred seventy.

113
00:05:38,441 --> 00:05:39,620
Question four.

114
00:05:40,370 --> 00:05:44,263
A plumber charges a fixed fee
for each job plus an hourly rate.

115
00:05:44,655 --> 00:05:46,921
A two hour job costs one
hundred ninety dollars,

116
00:05:46,941 --> 00:05:50,155
and a five hour job costs three
hundred eighty-five dollars.

117
00:05:50,655 --> 00:05:53,727
What is the plumber's
fixed fee, in dollars?

118
00:05:53,785 --> 00:05:54,856
Pause and try it.

119
00:05:58,100 --> 00:05:59,850
Treat each job as a point.

120
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,386
Two hours and one hundred ninety dollars.

121
00:06:02,743 --> 00:06:05,279
Five hours and three
hundred eighty-five dollars.

122
00:06:06,207 --> 00:06:08,242
The hourly rate is the slope.

123
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:12,636
The cost goes up one hundred ninety-five
dollars over three extra hours.

124
00:06:13,136 --> 00:06:15,243
That's sixty-five dollars per hour.

125
00:06:15,275 --> 00:06:17,847
The fixed fee is the cost at zero hours,

126
00:06:18,133 --> 00:06:19,275
the intercept.

127
00:06:19,561 --> 00:06:22,220
A two hour job includes two
hours at sixty-five dollars,

128
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,668
which is one hundred thirty.

129
00:06:23,739 --> 00:06:26,363
One hundred ninety minus
one hundred thirty is sixty.

130
00:06:26,383 --> 00:06:28,347
The fixed fee is sixty dollars.

131
00:06:28,375 --> 00:06:29,697
Check with the other job.

132
00:06:30,018 --> 00:06:34,212
Sixty plus five times sixty-five is
sixty plus three hundred twenty-five,

133
00:06:34,232 --> 00:06:35,640
which is three hundred eighty-five.

134
00:06:35,660 --> 00:06:40,962
The common mistake is dividing one hundred
ninety by two and calling ninety-five

135
00:06:40,982 --> 00:06:42,089
the hourly rate.

136
00:06:42,518 --> 00:06:43,875
That ignores the fee.

137
00:06:43,930 --> 00:06:45,323
Now inequalities.

138
00:06:46,573 --> 00:06:49,624
Watch for phrases like
at most, no more than,

139
00:06:49,644 --> 00:06:52,251
at least, and a minimum of.

140
00:06:52,536 --> 00:06:56,716
At most and no more than
mean less than or equal to.

141
00:06:57,144 --> 00:07:00,037
At least and a minimum of
mean greater than or equal to.

142
00:07:00,100 --> 00:07:01,672
Question five.

143
00:07:01,886 --> 00:07:05,188
A delivery van can carry at most
one thousand five hundred pounds,

144
00:07:05,208 --> 00:07:06,600
including the driver.

145
00:07:07,207 --> 00:07:09,243
The driver weighs one
hundred eighty pounds,

146
00:07:09,314 --> 00:07:11,815
and each box weighs forty-five pounds.

147
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:16,009
What is the greatest number of boxes
the van can carry on one trip with the

148
00:07:16,029 --> 00:07:16,836
driver?

149
00:07:16,856 --> 00:07:17,927
Pause and try it.

150
00:07:21,171 --> 00:07:22,600
Build it like an equation.

151
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:25,366
The driver, plus
forty-five pounds per box,

152
00:07:25,386 --> 00:07:28,064
has to be at most one
thousand five hundred.

153
00:07:28,136 --> 00:07:31,973
So one hundred eighty plus forty-five
b is less than or equal to one thousand

154
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:32,846
five hundred.

155
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:36,917
Subtract one hundred eighty, and
forty-five b is at most one thousand three

156
00:07:36,937 --> 00:07:38,009
hundred twenty.

157
00:07:38,509 --> 00:07:43,079
Divide by forty-five, and b is at
most about twenty-nine point three.

158
00:07:43,186 --> 00:07:47,401
You can't load part of a box, and thirty
boxes would put the van over the limit.

159
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:49,830
The answer is twenty-nine, choice A.

160
00:07:49,882 --> 00:07:51,990
Thirty is the rounding trap.

161
00:07:52,417 --> 00:07:55,454
Thirty-three and thirty-four
come from forgetting the driver.

162
00:07:56,240 --> 00:08:00,704
In Desmos, graph y equals one
hundred eighty plus forty-five x,

163
00:08:00,918 --> 00:08:02,327
and y equals one thousand five hundred.

164
00:08:02,347 --> 00:08:10,720
Zoom out and click the intersection:
about twenty-nine point three.

165
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,346
Twenty-nine is the last
whole number that fits.

166
00:08:13,389 --> 00:08:16,711
Question six, the hardest one.

167
00:08:17,246 --> 00:08:22,548
The function F of h equals forty-eight
minus one point five h gives the amount

168
00:08:22,568 --> 00:08:26,619
of fuel, in liters, in a generator's
tank h hours after the generator starts

169
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:27,298
running.

170
00:08:27,318 --> 00:08:28,675
Which statement is true?

171
00:08:28,731 --> 00:08:29,731
A.

172
00:08:30,088 --> 00:08:33,767
The fuel decreases by one point
five liters every forty minutes.

173
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:35,211
B.

174
00:08:35,231 --> 00:08:38,123
It decreases by one liter
every ninety minutes.

175
00:08:39,052 --> 00:08:39,318
C.

176
00:08:39,338 --> 00:08:41,695
The tank runs out after forty-eight hours.

177
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:42,747
D.

178
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:45,695
The fuel decreases by one
liter every forty minutes.

179
00:08:45,773 --> 00:08:46,916
Pause and try it.

180
00:08:47,702 --> 00:08:49,344
Take a little longer on this one.

181
00:08:53,553 --> 00:08:55,981
The slope is negative one point five,

182
00:08:56,016 --> 00:08:58,839
so the tank loses one point
five liters every hour.

183
00:09:00,838 --> 00:09:02,981
None of the choices say that directly.

184
00:09:03,767 --> 00:09:06,445
They restate the same
rate in different units.

185
00:09:07,016 --> 00:09:08,231
So convert.

186
00:09:08,286 --> 00:09:10,464
How long does it take to use one liter?

187
00:09:10,929 --> 00:09:14,357
One divided by one point five
is two thirds of an hour.

188
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,286
Two thirds of sixty
minutes is forty minutes.

189
00:09:17,464 --> 00:09:20,250
So the tank loses one
liter every forty minutes.

190
00:09:20,536 --> 00:09:23,107
The answer is D.

191
00:09:23,156 --> 00:09:24,243
A is the trap.

192
00:09:24,263 --> 00:09:26,993
It keeps one point five
liters but shortens the time,

193
00:09:27,013 --> 00:09:28,727
which makes the rate faster.

194
00:09:29,191 --> 00:09:32,206
B mixes up one point five
hours, which is ninety minutes,

195
00:09:32,226 --> 00:09:33,226
with the rate.

196
00:09:33,691 --> 00:09:37,834
And C treats forty-eight as a
time, but it's the starting fuel.

197
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:40,656
The tank runs out after thirty-two hours.

198
00:09:40,686 --> 00:09:44,988
For any rate in new units, convert every
choice back to the original units and

199
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:45,916
compare.

200
00:09:45,936 --> 00:09:50,595
One liter every forty minutes is
one liter per two thirds of an hour.

201
00:09:50,615 --> 00:09:52,630
That's one point five liters per hour.

202
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:53,864
It matches.

203
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:56,292
Here's the test-day method
for linear word problems.

204
00:09:56,312 --> 00:09:59,741
Step one: label the units.

205
00:10:00,241 --> 00:10:03,276
Write what x and y measure,
like hours and liters.

206
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:06,527
The slope's units are
always y units per x unit.

207
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:09,085
Step two: for an interpretation question,

208
00:10:09,105 --> 00:10:11,248
put the number into one
of the two sentences.

209
00:10:11,534 --> 00:10:16,300
For a slope: for each one more
x, y changes by this much.

210
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:19,712
For an intercept: when
x is zero, y is this.

211
00:10:20,034 --> 00:10:22,606
Then find the choice
that says the same thing.

212
00:10:22,635 --> 00:10:26,937
Step three: for building questions,
get the rate from two points first,

213
00:10:26,957 --> 00:10:28,957
then work back to the value at zero.

214
00:10:29,135 --> 00:10:32,544
For inequalities, translate at
most and at least carefully,

215
00:10:32,564 --> 00:10:35,099
and check whether the answer
has to be a whole number.

216
00:10:35,127 --> 00:10:36,127
Recap.

217
00:10:36,484 --> 00:10:39,806
Slope is a rate, in y units per x unit.

218
00:10:40,091 --> 00:10:43,377
The intercept is the starting
value, when x is zero.

219
00:10:43,484 --> 00:10:46,413
Find the rate from two
points before anything else.

220
00:10:46,591 --> 00:10:49,484
Convert rates that are
restated in new units.

221
00:10:49,913 --> 00:10:53,444
And round inequality answers in
the direction that keeps them true.

222
00:10:53,464 --> 00:10:57,464
Every question here was written for this
video in the style of the real test.

223
00:10:57,964 --> 00:11:02,050
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

224
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:04,143
skill, including linear functions.

225
00:11:04,221 --> 00:11:06,078
If this helped, subscribe.

226
00:11:06,935 --> 00:11:09,272
The next video switches
to Reading and Writing:

227
00:11:09,292 --> 00:11:13,042
rhetorical synthesis, the questions
built from a student's notes.
